 and other systems, and virtual and augmented reality training systems for the warfighter. In addition, It supplies turbine engines, engine components, accessories, and fuel management systems for PT6A, Twin-Pac, and JT15D aircraft engines. The company primarily serves national security-related agencies, the U.S. Department of Defense, intelligence and classified agencies, international government agencies, and domestic and international commercial customers. Kratos Defense & Security Solutions, Inc. was formerly known as Wireless Facilities, Inc. and changed its name to Kratos Defense & Security Solutions, Inc. in August 1999. Kratos Defense & Security Solutions, Inc. was incorporated in 1994 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","employees":4300,"website":"https://www.kratosdefense.com","country":"United States","city":"San Diego","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Eric M. DeMarco","title":"CEO, President & Director"},{"name":"Ms. Deanna Hom Lund CPA","title":"Executive VP, CFO & Director"},{"name":"Mr. Phillip  Carrai","title":"President of Space, Training & Cyber Solutions Division"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.0,"tpe":25.56,"ps":2.126,"pfcf":27.12,"peg":1.42,"pb":3.59,"ev_ebitda":14.49,"rev_growth":0.119,"eps_growth":0.1745,"eps_growth_fwd":0.156,"eps_growth_next":0.1437,"div_yield":0.007,"roe":0.1435,"roa":0.05694,"de":67.83,"gross_margin":0.319,"op_margin":0.1176,"profit_margin":0.0714,"current_ratio":1.724},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":null,"sector":18.0,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":289.6,"sector":25.56,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":3.973,"sector":2.126,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":-1,"sector":27.12,"verdict":"Negative FCF"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":null,"sector":1.42,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":1.89,"sector":3.59,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":7.128,"sector":67.83,"verdict":"Low debt"},{"k"